# vehje-fixpoint. relational engine

The framework's compile-stage engine: a generic, no-alloc, semi-naive
relational-fixpoint evaluator with congruence support, over caller-provided
columnar storage, deliberately free of any `vehje-ir` dependency. It reuses the
`hilavitkutin-api` columnar and `AccessSet` contracts as its storage vocabulary
and `arvo-graph` and `arvo-bitmask` as its algorithms, and adds the semi-naive
deltas, congruence closure, and provenance grades those do not carry. Three
clients define their own relation schemas over it: the lease and reachability
inference in `vehje-check`, the equality-saturation lowering in `vehje-lower`,
and the diagnostics witness reconstruction. The incremental scaling mechanism
is its differential layer. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
